{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792310860,"nonce":"ZVDLCel158+bJwXf6V0by3o7X1U=","title":"rayzor.test.Spec Mocha-style framework is built (single-file, core works) but BLOCKED as an imported lib by cross-module Dynamic-param ...","message":"**Session 2026-06-29: 5 prerequisite compiler bugs FIXED + committed (suite 153/153 green), then a test framework that stress-tested the cross-module subsystem.**\n\n- **5d23cff6**: (1) try/catch merge-phi — a var modified in a catch leaked to the\n  continuation when nothing threw (`try{pass+=1}catch{fail+=1}` gave fail=1);\n  build merge phis at the continuation (expression-arm lowering hir_to_mir ~20640,\n  and statement-form lower_try_catch). (2) `obj.fieldFn()` where fieldFn is a\n  function-typed DATA FIELD was dispatched as a (nonexistent) method → trap; now\n  lowered as an indirect call (resolve_function_typed_field, ast_lowering).\n- **d3c08ccc**: clone/copy UAF — `var b = a` for @:derive(Copy) freed the fresh\n  shallow copy (ownership-transfer block ran for a Copy binding); guard with\n  `copy_class_sym.is_none()`. See [[bugs_test_copy_clone_identity_flaky]].\n- **c643ec99**: (1) SAME-MODULE Dynamic boxing — primitive→Dynamic at call args\n  (maybe_materialize_for_call) + field stores (Assign Field lvalue). (2) subclass\n  alloc overflow — `class X extends ImportedClass` was undersized; the `stack`\n  field written at throw overflowed the heap. alloc_size_with_inheritance walks\n  the chain at `new`. This was the real root of test_exception's flaky exit-133\n  (NOT stub-stranding) — see [[bugs_test_exception_two_bugs]].\n\nMocha-style BDD: `describe`/`it`/`beforeEach`/`afterEach`/`expect(v).toEqual(...)`\n/`run():Int`. UNCOMMITTED. **CORE WORKS** (describe/it/run/report/beforeEach,\nclean failure messages via typed `catch(msg:String)`, failure detection) — verified.\nDesign notes that MATTER:\n- **MUST be a SINGLE FILE.** A multi-file package (Spec.hx + Expect.hx + Tier.hx)\n  SIGSEGV'd in `describe` before `body()` — cross-module/multi-file module-init\n  bug: an imported module that references sibling files in the same package\n  mis-initializes (the `prevSuite == \"\"` String compare derefs a bad ptr).\n  Consolidating all classes (Tier/Expect/TestCase/TestResult/Spec) into Spec.hx\n  fixed it. Imported single-file stdlib static initializers DO run correctly\n  (probed: `arr=[1,2,3]` len 3, `s=\"INIT\"` non-null).\n- Use typed `catch(e:String)` for assertion messages — `Std.string(e)` on a\n  Dynamic catch var holding a thrown String prints `\u003cunknown type N\u003e` (separate\n  open bug: thrown value not boxed as DynamicValue at the catch binding).\n\nThe narrow fix LANDED and the framework is COMMITTED (suite 154/154, the 20\nregressed tests all green). Framework works cross-module for **Int/Float/Bool/\nFloat** assertions (`Spec.expect(60).toEqual(60)`, `.toBeGreaterThan`, `.toBeTrue`)\nwith clean failure messages + failure detection. What made it work:\n- `boxing_param_types` (ast_lowering): import-aware formal-param resolution used\n  ONLY for the boxing decision — kept SEPARATE from the lambda-hint resolver\n  (`resolve_callee_formal_param_types`). Modifying the SHARED resolver was what\n  regressed ~20 tests (it perturbed closure-param inference — test_untyped_closure_\n  param_inference etc.). Static calls resolve via boxing_param_types (cross-module);\n  instance/same-module fall back to the existing `expected_arg_types` (read-only).\n- `coerce_arg_to_dynamic_param`: wraps a concrete value-type arg in `Cast{target:\n  Dynamic, kind:Implicit}`. MUST be `Implicit` (is_safe:true) — `Unsafe` casts to\n  Dynamic are a no-op reinterpret (hir_to_mir ~20196), they do NOT box.\n- **Restricted to Int/Float/Bool.** Adding String regressed the SAME 20 tests:\n  `trace` (and other Dynamic sinks) consume a RAW String pointer directly, so\n  boxing String args breaks them. String→Dynamic for Std.string is the remaining\n  gap (needs a tagged repr both trace and Std.string accept). So the framework's\n  STRING assertions (`expect(\"a\").toEqual(\"b\")`) still crash cross-module — use\n  numeric/bool for now.\n\n`Probe.show(42)` where show(x:Dynamic) is an IMPORTED method → the Int is passed\nRAW (not boxed), read back as a bogus DynamicValue → Std.string crashes. So the\nframework's `Spec.expect(60)` (cross-module, Int→Dynamic) crashes → framework\nunusable as an imported lib. SAME-module works (c643ec99). nue will hit this too.\n\n**ATTEMPTED FIX (reverted — DO NOT just re-apply):** TAST-layer coercion in\n`lower_call_expression` (ast_lowering): for each arg whose resolved formal param\nis Dynamic and arg is concrete, wrap in `Cast{target:Dynamic, kind:Implicit}` so\nhir_to_mir's Cast→Dynamic arm boxes it. Two sub-fixes were needed and WORKED\n(probe5 → \"got=42\", framework parts 1+2 passed):\n  1. `resolve_callee_formal_param_types` static-call branch used\n     `lookup_symbol(current_scope)` which MISSES imported classes; added\n     `resolve_class_like_symbol_by_name` fallback.\n  2. `CastKind::Unsafe` is a no-op reinterpret (NOT boxing) — `is_safe:false` casts\n     to Dynamic are treated as identity (hir_to_mir ~20196). Must use\n     `CastKind::Implicit` (is_safe:true) to hit the boxing arm (~20232).\n**BUT it caused a 20-test SIGSEGV regression** (test_simd16i8_*, test_q4km_*,\ngenerics, reflection, arrays — all 139 --no-cache). Root: over-boxing args whose\nformal resolves to Dynamic via TYPE-PARAMS / abstracts / FFI handles (SIMD/quant/\nPtr), and/or the broadened resolver perturbing the shared expected_arg_types\n(lambda-hint) path. REVERTED to restore green.\n\n**Right next approach (focused session + full regression matrix):** narrow the\ncoercion HARD — only box when formal is the genuine `Dynamic` type (not a\ntype-param-resolved-to-Dynamic; guard against generic/abstract/coreType params),\nlikely only value types (Int/Float/Bool). Separate the