(boxed, fine) — class\n  instances as Dynamic args to cross-module instance methods don't survive.\n- `Reflect.fields(primitive)` / deepEquals on primitives **crashes** cross-module\n  (static `fieldCount`/`fieldVal` worked, but the recursive deepEquals path crashed).\n- `Std.isOfType(obj, Cls)` returns **false for the correct class** cross-module\n  (same-module true) — class identity lost across the boundary.\n- `Type.typeof(v)`+`Std.string` → **W0020 SIGILL stub** cross-module (lowering gap),\n  poisons the caller too.\nSo I did NOT add toBe/toEqualDeep/toBeInstanceOf/toBeOfType — they'd be hidden\nerrors. Framework stays VALUE (`expect`: Int/Float/Bool/structural-by-Std.string)\n+ STRING (`expectStr`). These four are real cross-module Dynamic-object/reflection\ncompiler bugs (the dangerous subsystem); they'd bite nue only if it does\ncross-module Dynamic reflection/downcasts (it mostly uses typed Tensors +\nSys.println, so largely unaffected). Also: nested-closure capture of an outer\nlocal through `describe(()-\u003e{ it(()-\u003e...outerLocal...) })` → **E0100** (loud, not\nhidden) — framework tests must build their objects INSIDE the `it` body.\n\nUser wants `@tier` conditional compilation via the PREPROCESSOR, not a runtime\n`activeTier` var (which ALSO failed: cross-module static WRITE `Spec.activeTier =\nTier.JIT` from Main didn't persist — another x-module static gap). `#if jit/#else/\nuser `extra_defines`; there is NO `-D` CLI flag and NO per-backend tier define.\nPLAN: in main.rs run/aot handlers, derive a tier symbol from the command/flags\n(run→`jit`, aot or --llvm or tier3→`llvm`, tier0→`interp`) and push to\nextra_defines so `#if jit` activates. rayzor's tiered JIT is DYNAMIC (interp→\ncranelift→llvm at runtime), so \"tier\" for tests = the execution MODE the harness\npicks, not a fixed compile-time tier.\n\n---\nArchived from Claude memory `project_rayzor_test_framework_and_xmodule_dynamic` on 2026-10-18. A record of past work; open items in it may have their own issues.","files":null}]}